{
 "_note": "Crafting paths for FAMILY MEMBERS (followers keep their NPC classes). Each path ranks Apprentice→Journeyman→Master→Grandmaster by path XP (earned 1:1 from XP in the path's skills) plus a skill gate. A member starts one main path; every rank gained anywhere opens one more slot (up to maxPaths). Secondary paths are capped at secondaryGap below the main path. At specAt (Master) a path offers ONE specialty, which ranks the same way (capped at the path's rank). fx values scale by (rank+1). Add a path by appending here (e.g. Jeweler, Scribe): engine and UI read this list. comboPaths: `requires` is a list of {path,rank} | {path,spec} | {skill,lvl} | {classLine} (adventuring class line, e.g. apprentice = mage line) on ONE member; Scribe (business, drafting, writing) is an input of every combo; combos have their own ranks and specialties, never use a path slot, are uncapped, and never block their input paths. openCredit: share of the XP already in the path's best skill credited when the path is opened. Ladder: base ranks → specialty (at specAt) → artisan title (spec rank artisanAt, specs with an `artisan` block: new name, fx ×artisanMult). Merges (path.merges): a Grandmaster specialty listed in a merge may take the other one as spec2; Grandmaster in both gives the merged title. R46: maxPaths/secondaryGap are replaced by `slots` (main/secondary/gathering/dabbling); path `kind` is crafting or gathering.",
